Answer: Many products can belong to one category, so a @ManyToOne relationship can be used:

```java
@ManyToOne
@JoinColumn(name = "category_id")
private Category category;
```

A category can contain many products through a corresponding @OneToMany relationship.

Answer: Validation can be added to the DTO or entity:

```java
@Positive
private BigDecimal price;
@PositiveOrZero
private Integer stock;
```

The service should also validate these values because business rules should not depend only on frontend validation.

Answer: A cart can contain multiple cart items, so it is normally a one-to-many relationship:

```java
@OneToMany(mappedBy = "cart", cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
private List<CartItem> items;
```

Each CartItem usually contains a product ID, quantity, and possibly a price snapshot.

Answer: One order can contain many order items, so it is a one-to-many relationship:

```java
@OneToMany(mappedBy = "order", cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
private List<OrderItem> items;
```

Each order item records the purchased product, quantity, and purchase price.

